2026-08-24T11:22:38.556+05:30  INFO 14148 --- [doc-mind] [http-nio-8080-exec-5] c.p.d.ai.provider.NvidiaModelService     : Response: QueryResponse[message=Java fundamentals covered in the document include: core language concepts such as the difference between == (reference/primitive comparison) and equals (logical equality); collection framework differences like ArrayList (dynamic array, fast indexed access) vs LinkedList (linked nodes, good for deque operations), and HashMap (non-thread-safe) vs ConcurrentHashMap (thread-safe, scalable); concurrency primitives including synchronized (mutual exclusion and visibility) vs volatile (visibility and ordering without atomicity), Runnable (no result) vs Callable (returns result, throws checked exceptions), Future (blocking get) vs CompletableFuture (composable async pipelines), and thread pool management via ExecutorService (FixedThreadPool, ScheduledExecutorService); object-oriented principles like interface (contract) vs abstract class (shared state/implementation); dependency injection (providing dependencies externally) with constructor injection preferred; equals/hashCode contract (equal objects must have same hashCode, same hashCode doesn't imply equality); exception handling with try/catch/finally/throw/throws, checked (compile-time enforced, e.g., IOException) vs unchecked exceptions (RuntimeException subclasses, e.g., NullPointerException), try-with-resources for AutoCloseable resources, and custom exceptions; threading model with Thread, atomic operations (AtomicInteger), and explicit locking (ReentrantLock); and a glossary of common acronyms (JVM, JDK, JRE, OOP, API, REST, HTTP, HTTPS, JPA, ORM, IoC, DI, RAG, LLM, AI, NLP, JWT, OAuth2, OIDC, TLS, CORS, CSRF, XSS, SQL, ACID, CRUD, CI, CD).]
